      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Looking at it from a game designer&#39;s perspective, there are clear signs that Omnitron-X and Omnitron-IV were both built with the explicit intention of having interesting interactions with other Omnitrons.</p><p>See also Grand Warlord Voss and the Dok&#39;Thorath Capitol.&nbsp; The keywords Minion and Thorathian suddenly become much... denser when both are in play.</p><p>By contrast, the game designer does not sanction having multiple variants of the same hero deck in play at once.&nbsp; If you want Legacy, Young Legacy and Old Legacy all in the same game, you need to use house rules (and have extra copies of the Legacy deck!).&nbsp; You can, of course, have any one version of Legacy go up against Iron Legacy, just like you can have Visionary fight The Dreamer.</p>",
