    {
      "id": 138277,
      "name": "AlexxKay",
      "username": "AlexxKay",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-30T00:52:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Elcarp\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/e19adc/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Elcarp:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That makes sense. What about my first question? Is it even allowed officially to have them in the same game, or is it akin to multiple of the same hero? Technically all three are the same being, just different incarnations of him.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Whatever the timeline fiction says, the real restriction is that you can only have one copy of a given DECK in a game.&nbsp; As long as the 'alternate' version has its own unique deck (not just a variant Hero card), it's allowed.</p>",
