      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"AlexxKay\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> AlexxKay:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div>Whatever the timeline fiction says, the real restriction is that you can only have one copy of a given DECK in a game.&nbsp; As long as the 'alternate' version has its own unique deck (not just a variant Hero card), it's allowed.<br>&nbsp;</div>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>So because they are in fact a hero deck, a villian deck, and an environment deck, they affect each other in terms of \"drone\" and \"component\" cards, but they are all allowed in the same game?</p>",
