    {
      "id": 138283,
      "name": "Agent Bon",
      "username": "Agent_Bon",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/13edae/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-30T21:34:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"AlexxKay\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> AlexxKay:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>…the game designer does not sanction having multiple variants of the same hero deck in play at once.  If you want Legacy, Young Legacy and Old Legacy all in the same game, you need to use house rules (and have extra copies of the Legacy deck!).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I remember Christopher saying that you could have multiple variations, but that you could only have one of each limited among all of them.  No stacking multiple copies of Inspiring Presence.  I can’t remember what thread it was but it was on the forums.</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:14:47.716Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
